<p>Summoned via PM.</p>
<p>I'll start with the big problem I see with this. You have listed the central narrative as none. While an article doesn't need a narrative to be successful, most articles contain a strong narrative with their anomaly to draw attention and strengthen the piece. Without a narrative, you really aren't selling your idea to its full potential. That would be my first suggestion, and number one thing to work on. I would check out the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/guide-hub">Guide Hub</a> for a list of helpful articles that will assist in this endeavor.</p>
<p>As for the anomaly, its rather vague. You mention its a space time anomaly, and then do not detail it any further. You then try to tie it into another SCP article which really isn't recommended for a first time article. I suggest expanding on the vagueness of your idea, giving it detail and depth so that readers may understand what it does.</p>
<p>I would also suggest not linking a sandbox here on the idea forums. You should be able to effectively outline your idea within the format given. Reviewers have no obligation to check it, and usually don't on the idea thread. Best of luck.</p>

