In the year 2059, multiple sightings of strange shadows resembling in behaviour and nature to the shadows of the SCP are confirmed around the globe. It is suggested that the shadows travelled through the void of space from the SCP to Earth to hunt for prey. While this threatens all the life on this planet, it leaves the SCP itself vulnerable. So, the Foundation comes up with a plan. Try put up a small resistance and feed the shadows to keep them occupied while the combined forces of the Foundation and several nations prepare an attack on the SCP.<br />
The plan is to send a crew ito the wormhole and put a reality anchor inside. This will make the nebula to lose its anomalous properties and just pass Eath without anything really happening besides a small cloudy weather. However, they do not know that some shadows stills reside inside the wormhole. If they were to fail, a whole planetary evacuation would take place by orders for the O5 Council. They eventually succeed, and the rest of the Foundation’s forces destroy any remaining shadows on Earth that are confused by the lack of command from the wormhole, but one thing's sure, it's gonna be a massacre.<br />
<strong>Edit:</strong> Just wanted to mention that if you’re wondering why didn’t The Foundation put a reality anchor earlier, and why they waited that the anomaly gets close to do it, is because the shadows wouldn’t even let them get close, they already tried it anyways and failed, twice. So now that the shadows are on Earth, there is a chance.</p>

