<p>Whilst this makes sense in terms of wanting to increase the human elements of the story, it is very tacked on. The central story here is focused on how the Foundation deals with this ticking timebomb and taking time (heh) out of that to focus on citizen characters who have no bearing on the final outcome of the narrative will hurt the pacing a lot. If it's not feeding into some aspect of the overall plot, it's not useful to include it, and although this does serve to cement some of the horror and terror of the anomaly, it's otherwise pretty insubstantial.</p>
