			<div class="content" id="post-content-4797462">
									

<p>Please please please don't do this. This is another catch-all tool Macguffin similar to a reality anchor but introduces way more problems than it fixes.</p>
<p>SRAs only survive because no one ever tries to explain <em>how</em> they work. The more information you give us, the more questions you open yourself up to. On the flipside, if you don't provide enough information, then there are still questions.</p>
<p>It's a delicate balance. But stringing together disparate scientific buzzwords in an attempt to build a Macguffin is <em>not</em> the solution. That's not what dark energy is, that's not what antimatter is, and neither of those relate to any sort of quantum destabilisation.</p>
<p>If dark energy (which accounts for 70% of the energy density of the universe at present) generated antimatter (which isn't all that special, it's just particles that happen to annihilate with regular matter) then there wouldn't be&#8230; <em>anything</em>. Just photons. Antimatter isn't all that interesting, and things like positrons (the antimatter electron, which is just an electron with a positive charge and opposite polarity) are emitted fairly regularly via the electroweak process.</p>

